  "title": "Why must area below the time axis count as negative?",
  "body": " Why must area below the time axis count as negative?   On a velocity graph, a rectangle below the time axis has ordinary geometric area that is positive. In your own words, why does calculus assign that region a negative signed area anyway?    Signed area is not painting a wall. It is accumulating change, and backward motion decreases position.   "
