  "body": " How does the picture match the definition?   The definition says that every horizontal band around must contain the graph over some punctured vertical strip around . In your own words, why does a jump fail this picture, and why can one-sided versions still succeed when the two-sided test fails?    A two-sided strip has to control both sides at once. If the two sides head toward different heights, no single band around one target can hold both nearby pieces. A one-sided test only looks at one half of the strip.   "
