  "title": "What does a cutoff index <span class=\"process-math\">\\(N\\)<\/span> do in place of a <span class=\"process-math\">\\(\\delta\\text{?}\\)<\/span>",
  "body": " What does a cutoff index do in place of a ?   Sequence convergence uses the same epsilon idea, but the response is a whole-number cutoff: after , every term stays inside the -window around . In your own words, why does the order first , then still matter, and what would it mean for a sequence to diverge?    The challenger still names any positive output error. You answer with how far out in the list you must go. Divergence means no finite target survives every such challenge, whether by oscillation or by growing without bound.   "
