  "title": "Why can a trigonometric-substitution triangle fail on another interval?",
  "body": " Why can a trigonometric-substitution triangle fail on another interval?   A formula derived from with is built for . In your own words, why can blindly reusing that formula for change the answer, and what does that say about indefinite integrals on disconnected domains?    A triangle carries sign information. Separate pieces of the domain, such as and , may need different ranges or different inverse functions.   "
