  "body": " Why does Simpson’s error bound involve the fourth derivative?   Midpoint and trapezoidal errors are controlled by . Simpson’s bound is controlled by and shrinks like . In your own words, why does exactness through cubics push the first possible error to the next derivative, and why is a bound still only a guarantee?    A rule that is exact for polynomials up through degree first feels the failure of a degree- term. Doubling divides the bound by , but the actual error may be smaller.   "
