  "body": " When is an implicit equation a legitimate solution?   Separation may produce a relation such as instead of a formula . In your own words, why can that still be a solution, and why is a formula without a domain still incomplete?    Differentiating the implicit relation can recover the differential equation. A solution must live on an interval where the function is differentiable and the original equation makes sense.   "
