  "title": "Why does damping drain energy?",
  "body": " Why does damping drain energy?   A damping force opposing velocity produces . In your own words, why does that term make oscillation fade, and what role do complex characteristic roots play in describing the faded motion?    Negative derivative of energy means the energy is decreasing whenever the mass is moving. Light damping gives complex roots whose real part produces exponential decay multiplying the oscillation.   "
