  "body": " Circles  A circle is a distance condition.  Choose a center   and a radius . A point lies on the circle if its distance from is exactly .  That sentence becomes an equation.   Equation of a circle  The distance from to is   So the circle condition is   Squaring both sides gives   This is the standard equation of a circle with center and radius .  If the center is the origin, the equation becomes    Example   Find an equation of the circle with center   and radius   Use the standard form:   Thus    The circle has center and radius .          Completing the square  A circle is not always written in standard form. Completing the square reveals the center and radius.   Example   Show that   is a circle, and find its center and radius.  Group the -terms and -terms:   Complete the square in each variable:   and   Substitute:   Thus   So the center is   and the radius is       Disks and circle inequalities  A circle is the boundary. A disk is the filled-in region.  The equation   means distance exactly from .  The inequality   means distance less than . This is the inside of the circle, without the boundary.  The inequality   means the inside together with the boundary.     condition  region     circle     inside, boundary excluded     inside, boundary included     outside, boundary excluded      Example   Describe the region   The center is   and the radius is   Because the inequality is , the region is the closed disk: all points whose distance from is at most .     "
